#   ..._fresh_lines_on_an_unchanged_step_report_no_progress          A-025's second case
#   ..._no_ledger_at_all_is_an_empty_roster_not_an_error             CT-004's empty input
#
# FR-025's derivation is pinned by the four threshold_* names: the constant is
# above 5x the shortest measured working batch and below half the median, so
# retuning it to a "generic constant" turns them red.
#
# GRIND cycle 4 added two sections. D-022 — a finished agent stops writing, so
# without a terminal state it ages into `stalled` and silts up needs_attention
# until the list stops being read:
#   ..._a_finished_agent_reports_done_however_long_ago_it_finished  the defect
#   ..._a_finished_agent_does_not_fill_needs_attention              its real cost
#   ..._a_resumed_agent_leaves_done_behind          terminal is the LAST line,
#                                                   not a latch on the file
# D-021 — the four INSPECT stream agents are spawned from the F2 roster, not
# from either tool in this module, so a glob over progress/ had no row for
# them at all and their silence was indistinguishable from success:
#   ..._expected_stream_agents_with_no_ledger_are_reported        the defect
#   ..._a_missing_stream_record_carries_the_block_that_fixes_it   the remedy
#                                                                 travels with it
#   ..._streams_are_not_expected_outside_inspect     and the guards against the
#   ..._a_just_spawned_stream_is_not_yet_late        permanent false alarm that
#   ..._conditional_streams_are_only_expected_...    would rebuild D-022
#
# GRIND cycle 5 added the D-058 section. The roster was built from the ledger
# files that EXIST plus an expected-STREAM set, so a teammate the run had
# dispatched which died before writing line one contributed to neither half:
# it was absent from the report and needs_attention said nothing was wrong.
# The roster now also reads spawns.log, the run's own record of what it
# dispatched. Read these first:
#   ..._a_teammate_that_died_before_line_one_is_on_the_roster   the defect, in
#                                                   the F1 scenario PROVE drove
#   ..._a_redispatched_agent_stops_reading_as_finished   the same invisibility
#                                                   one dispatch on: a stale
#                                                   terminal line no longer
#                                                   retires a re-dispatched agent
#   ..._a_dispatched_teammate_with_a_ledger_appears_exactly_once   the two halves
#                                                   of the roster key agents
#                                                   identically or one agent
#                                                   becomes two rows
# And the four guards against rebuilding D-022's silting, which pass both
# before and after the fix precisely because they pin what must NOT change:
